{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support","id":494360,"title":"If Dark Ages got returning support","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T21:48:37-07:00","id":494360,"title":"If Dark Ages got returning support","content":"What books would you like to see for expanding to existing Dark Ages lines?<br /> <br /> Top of my list would be Dark Ages: Djinn, taking a look at the Arabian cousins of the Fae, and their court &amp; Dominion system as differed by their metaphysical different relationship to religion (possibly as imposed on them by Suleiyman - it depends on who you believe, Djinn of Faith say it was their willingness to bow to Adam at the dawn of days that gave them moral souls without Locking them), and some overlap with the Umbra on their part + Umbral relatives (to stay consistent with Djinn as presented in Dark Ages: Mage... Taftani can actually get a full Fellowship writeup here as well).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T01:00:29-07:00","id":494504,"title":"","content":"Djinn were never presented as Fae in the old WoD, though. They were always spirits, and the best look we got at them was in the Lost Paths book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T01:32:18-07:00","id":494515,"title":"","content":"How about a Dark Ages: Wraith? In our current Vampire story, the notion of cultural funeral rites and the consequences of improper burial have been really delicious. I can think of a lot of stories I want to tell about the restless dead this deep into history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:54:18-07:00","id":494969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>warmerdutch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=494515#post494515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Dark Ages: Wraith? In our current Vampire story, the notion of cultural funeral rites and the consequences of improper burial have been really delicious. I can think of a lot of stories I want to tell about the restless dead this deep into history.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Wraith</i> actually covers what was going on in Stygia and the Shadowlands during the Dark Ages time period, so other than maybe a few Arcanos tweaks, I don't think there's much possibility for story there - at least not enough to warrant its own book.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:03:59-07:00","id":494980,"title":"","content":"I vote for Dark Ages Wraith as well. Mage the Ascension has a lot of flavor text about what happened at the founding of the Traditions and the Order of Reason and how things went in the early days, but that doesn't mean that Sorcerer's Crusade wasn't worthwhile for almost all values of worthiness. Even if we have a simple outline of what Charon was doing at the time, it was still a very different set-up from modern Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T12:52:42-07:00","id":495101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=494969#post494969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Wraith</i> actually covers what was going on in Stygia and the Shadowlands during the Dark Ages time period, so other than maybe a few Arcanos tweaks, I don't think there's much possibility for story there - at least not enough to warrant its own book.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guilds operating openly, a civil war brewing because of the Fishers heretic cult, and massive turmoil in the undescribed Middle Eastern shadowlands isn't enough for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T14:21:17-07:00","id":495190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=494504#post494504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Djinn were never presented as Fae in the old WoD, though. They were always spirits, and the best look we got at them was in the Lost Paths book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's ridiculous because Djinn and Fae have identical stories except for their relationship to monotheism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:10:13-07:00","id":495257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495190#post495190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that's ridiculous because Djinn and Fae have identical stories except for their relationship to monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in theory, but I expect any game based on the Djinn would be about as different from Changeling as Land of 8 Milllion Dreams is from normal Changeling. And these Djinn would not be the same Djinn of the Taftani and Mage. The concept of Djinn as spirits is perfect for the Taftani, the Batini, the Lions and the Hermetics, who perceive the whole thing through the keys of Solomon and the binding of the Efreet to the will of the Magi. The Spirit sphere just screams Solomonic magic.<br /> <br /> Of course Djinn as Changeling would work great, but it would be a very weird take on Changeling. It's a thing that was broached in Changeling the Lost, but I would have preffered a deep, unorthodox fluff rich take that White Wolf was well known for. I'd have been the first in line to grab that book. Also, do consider that not all Djinn are bound by Allah or even serve Allah. Some of them are just plain bastards and serve the same roles which would be fulfilled by devils or monsters in other cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:36:56-07:00","id":495317,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages: Wraith and Dark Ages: Changeling (NOT DA: Fae, but something that really connects and serves as a prequel to CtD line).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:55:43-07:00","id":495335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495317#post495317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Ages: Wraith and Dark Ages: Changeling (NOT DA: Fae, but something that really connects and serves as a prequel to CtD line).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Faeries explicitly born from human dreams would be grossly out of theme in the Dark Ages setting - it's such a modern concept of the supernatural. DA: Fae IS the CtD canonical prequel, as Darkening Sky shows how the weaponized Echoes (*cough*Banality*cough*) of the returned War of the Seasons results in the changing of the nature of the Fae to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:20:27-07:00","id":495364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495101#post495101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guilds operating openly, a civil war brewing because of the Fishers heretic cult, and massive turmoil in the undescribed Middle Eastern shadowlands isn't enough for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I meant more &quot;There's not really any big mystery that hasn't been documented&quot; rather than &quot;There's no story hooks.&quot; True, it would be an interesting setting to play in, but that's something that solved with a bit of research rather than printing an official book.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:29:57-07:00","id":496371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495257#post495257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree in theory, but I expect any game based on the Djinn would be about as different from Changeling as Land of 8 Milllion Dreams is from normal Changeling. And these Djinn would not be the same Djinn of the Taftani and Mage. The concept of Djinn as spirits is perfect for the Taftani, the Batini, the Lions and the Hermetics, who perceive the whole thing through the keys of Solomon and the binding of the Efreet to the will of the Magi. The Spirit sphere just screams Solomonic magic.<br /> <br /> Of course Djinn as Changeling would work great, but it would be a very weird take on Changeling. It's a thing that was broached in Changeling the Lost, but I would have preffered a deep, unorthodox fluff rich take that White Wolf was well known for. I'd have been the first in line to grab that book. Also, do consider that not all Djinn are bound by Allah or even serve Allah. Some of them are just plain bastards and serve the same roles which would be fulfilled by devils or monsters in other cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't a huge chunk of the djinn go and follow Ibilis? It does seem like it might be an interesting game supplement to have out there. If Veil of Night can get it's own hardback back in the day, the Djinn should be worth a product on the order of Land of 8 Million Dreams. They definitely have a few factions and come in several different types and coming up with mechanisms for what they do in the relevant tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:53:53-07:00","id":496392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495364#post495364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I meant more &quot;There's not really any big mystery that hasn't been documented&quot; rather than &quot;There's no story hooks.&quot; True, it would be an interesting setting to play in, but that's something that solved with a bit of research rather than printing an official book.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Stygia was definitely a different place. The &quot;Heretics&quot;, particularly the Fishers aren't heretical and are a major part of the cultural landscape. So the mystery of what exactly is going on with the Far Shores and how that ties into Transcendence is out there. The Guilds are rolling along full force with all their myriad little issues, though they aren't exactly organized as guilde yet er se, so there is a wide variety of organizations and associations dealing with the Arcanoi. The last Great Maelstrom was hundreds of years ago and the next one was hundreds of years off. Like World War I, they probably didn't think there was going to BE another Great Maelstrom. The Deathlords might have been more wraith-wranglers and bureaucrats than petty militaristic autocrats.<br /> <br /> I doubt that it wouldn't be any more similar to the situation in modern Wraith than Vampire Dark Ages (which could just as easily have been, &quot;lets just have a Winds of East size book with one page write-ups of the Cappadocians and Salubri in it&quot;) would be to modern Vampire or DA Werewolf to Apocalypse though perhaps not as different as DA Mage and DA Fae are to their respective descendants. <br /> <br /> DA Wraith is the &quot;big hole&quot; in the DA setting. All the other mainline games have some kind of DA &quot;reflection&quot;. (Devil's Due for DtF is the most tenuous, but that's built into the nature of DtF). I guess the Mummies could have more than a couple of pages in Veil of Night, but it might be difficult to get something like Blood &amp; Silk out of the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T11:12:55-07:00","id":496497,"title":"","content":"@Ajax See, that's an interesting setting to play in, and I would love to play in it, but you've summed it all up in what, a paragraph? I just don't feel the need for an &quot;official book.&quot; Maybe if it had a dual focus, like detailing the Far Shores as well (in fact, I would love a Far Shores source book disguised as <i>Dark Ages: Wraith</i>), or something like that. But just &quot;Here is Stygia in the Dark Ages. The Dark Ages line is now complete&quot; does not fascinate me.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:11:45-07:00","id":496671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495257#post495257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course Djinn as Changeling would work great, but it would be a very weird take on Changeling. It's a thing that was broached in Changeling the Lost, but I would have preffered a deep, unorthodox fluff rich take that White Wolf was well known for. I'd have been the first in line to grab that book. Also, do consider that not all Djinn are bound by Allah or even serve Allah. Some of them are just plain bastards and serve the same roles which would be fulfilled by devils or monsters in other cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>That' exactly what I'm proposing. A book that covers the relatives of the Fae with their own Courts and Domains and systems and culture.<br /> <br /> And I know not all Djinn are bound by or serve Allah. My point was that that relationship actively divides them (i.e. those who are religious, those who follow Iblis, etc); as opposed to Fae to whom Monotheism is inherently anathemic, and are generally seen as morally completely outside of the human condition of Original Sin and Salvation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T16:13:23-07:00","id":496861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495335#post495335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Faeries explicitly born from human dreams would be grossly out of theme in the Dark Ages setting - it's such a modern concept of the supernatural. DA: Fae IS the CtD canonical prequel, as Darkening Sky shows how the weaponized Echoes (*cough*Banality*cough*) of the returned War of the Seasons results in the changing of the nature of the Fae to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know what you mean, but still, I don't feel confortable considering DA: Fae as a canonical prequel (not even the creators, as they pulled out this idea while promoting this title). I don't care that much that Medieval concept of faeries wasn't connected to dreams and nightmares or if it would have had been out of theme in DA setting, because since CtD deals with that, I think it woud be interesting to CtD line (which is more important to me as primarily a CtD Storyteller and Player, and not a DA player). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:09:50-07:00","id":497640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=496497#post496497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ajax See, that's an interesting setting to play in, and I would love to play in it, but you've summed it all up in what, a paragraph? I just don't feel the need for an &quot;official book.&quot; Maybe if it had a dual focus, like detailing the Far Shores as well (in fact, I would love a Far Shores source book disguised as <i>Dark Ages: Wraith</i>), or something like that. But just &quot;Here is Stygia in the Dark Ages. The Dark Ages line is now complete&quot; does not fascinate me.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've pointed out some huge areas that are different and could be explored that I came up with off the top of my head without even getting up and going into my office and looking at a single Wraith book. Plus whatever weirdness they come up with. Using your logic, Wraith the Great War should never have happened at all, because it could be handled with &quot;The War really sucked. There was a Maelstrom it sucked so bad. The Grim Legion and the Skeletal Legions got big because of war and disease.&quot; Or, more to the point, Vampire the Dark Ages could just be: &quot;All the same Clans except no Giovanni. Replace with Cappadocians. Lower technology. Done.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T12:41:10-07:00","id":497739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=497640#post497640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, more to the point, Vampire the Dark Ages could just be: &quot;All the same Clans except no Giovanni. Replace with Cappadocians. Lower technology. Done.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying this as a fan and backer of V20DA and owner of the deluxe VDA book, but isn't that exactly what DAV <i>is</i>?<br /> <br /> Really, it just boils down to the fact that I don't feel an <u>official</u> book is necessary; if I want to set a <i>Wraith</i> game in the Dark Ages, I'll do so without a book. I don't need the rubber stamp of validation on a setting, I just do the research. That and I've never understood the fascination with Dark Ages as a <i>line</i>; the original intent was for each line to have a &quot;signature setting&quot; - Wild West for <i>Werewolf</i>, Great War for <i>Wraith</i>, the Sorcerer's Crusade stuff for Mage (which is a whole other discussion), and whatever Changeling had. Somehow Dark Ages became a thing and Vampire got Victorian Age as its new &quot;signature setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, as I've said, I don't think there's a lot of mystery involved in the Dark Ages setting for <i>Wraith</i>. the timeline in the Wraith books gives details about the major events that happened, whereas the timelines in <i>Masquerade</i> usually said really vague things, like &quot;The War of Princes happened. Then the Inquisition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":".  This site is not friendly with mobile devices. 04-30-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:21:17-07:00","id":498299,"title":"","content":"Wrath and Changeling have always been in the shadows of the other lines. First a Dark Ages Wraith book as a setting might be useful not necessary. The society in Wraith if I recall correctly is entering a major social upheaval the Guilds are about to be outlawed, The Fishers over thrown, and the Far Isles cut adrift. While I'm certain that I could using the Wraith main book cobble together a campaign, change the arcanoi as needed and write a fairly compelling story it would be far easier for both my players and myself if I could just hand them a book with the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:52:17-07:00","id":502054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495190#post495190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's ridiculous because Djinn and Fae have identical stories except for their relationship to monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. There is a lot of overlap. Both faeries and djinn are invisible people that live alongside humanity who have wonderful powers, and can be beneficial or malevolent. It's the same concept, different name. If I ever ran a game where it would be important, I'd make most of the Djinn out of the Changeling Kiths (Sidhe for Marid, Trolls for Efreeti, Sluagh and Redcaps as Ghuls, athe others as Jann.)<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't stop Spirits also being djinn any more than it stopped certain European faeries from being classed as Spirits in various Werewolf or Marge books. And plasmic creatures with that name would still dwell in the Tempest like the Angelics and Demonics do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Djinn&quot; is a loose enough concept that it can cover a lot.<br /> <br /> What I don't see the need for is to constantly reinvent the wheel every time someone expands the setting into a different part of the world. For that matter, I don't see the reason for different Kiths for the Nunnehi. Archetypes should be strong enough to allow their use in any culture with only some basic changes in &quot;social structure&quot; to better simulate that cultural traditions stories of the little people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T22:48:16-07:00","id":502534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=494504#post494504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Djinn were never presented as Fae in the old WoD, though. They were always spirits, and the best look we got at them was in the Lost Paths book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No they were presented as weird bygones that were kind of spirity. DA Fae suggests they are fae though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T18:15:54-07:00","id":503698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=495101#post495101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guilds operating openly, a civil war brewing because of the Fishers heretic cult, and massive turmoil in the undescribed Middle Eastern shadowlands isn't enough for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. The number one item on my wish list for a renewed <b>Dark Ages</b> line would be <b>Wraith</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:57:53-07:00","id":504382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=496861#post496861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you mean, but still, I don't feel confortable considering DA: Fae as a canonical prequel (not even the creators, as they pulled out this idea while promoting this title). I don't care that much that Medieval concept of faeries wasn't connected to dreams and nightmares or if it would have had been out of theme in DA setting, because since CtD deals with that, I think it woud be interesting to CtD line (which is more important to me as primarily a CtD Storyteller and Player, and not a DA player). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that if DA: Fae gets revisited it'll be similar to how V20 Dark Ages is a V20 supplement instead of the core book for a Dark Ages game line. That being said, I also hope that it doesn't change too much about the setup of DA: Fae. I like that it presents Fae society before the shattering but are confused about the new found power humans seem to have which any Changeling: The Dreaming fan can immediately recognize as the rise of banality during the sundering. My only compliant is that I wish it tied into established C:tD history a little better. There's no mention of the Fomorians or the noble houses for example. The DA: Fae scenario in Darkening Sky, despite my dislike of it as a pre-made adventure, the trigger for the Shattering was brilliant. Hopefully, if future DA: Fae material is a C20 supplement, it'll tie into C:tD's established history a bit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:11:33-07:00","id":504483,"title":"","content":"Considering how well V20: DA did, my guess is we'll probably see W20 and maybe M20 get Dark Ages books announced at GenCon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:36:27-07:00","id":504682,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see those two get a complete overhall. Werewolf needs to move further from the &quot;present&quot; setting and play up the different type of stories to tell in the setting. Mage is good setting-wise, but suffers from the problem of reducing an entire range of magic withing a pardigm to four pillars, means that the overlap of capabilities is MASSIVE. To make characters more distinct, I'd make knowing specific &quot;spells&quot; (rotes) actually matter, thus playing up the studying magical lore element of the setting. Basically I'd rip off DA: Fae a bit, and make spells you know easier and safer, while creative casting has huge backlash risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:18:03-07:00","id":504814,"title":"","content":"You'd get a few thousand comments easily on fights about crossover rules, I'd imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:24:49-07:00","id":504830,"title":"","content":"I'd love a M20<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A book, personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=504682#post504682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make characters more distinct, I'd make knowing specific &quot;spells&quot; (rotes) actually matter, thus playing up the studying magical lore element of the setting. Basically I'd rip off DA: Fae a bit, and make spells you know easier and safer, while creative casting has huge backlash risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great idea. Whether they do a new DA book for Mage or not, consider it stolen and implemented. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:01:39-07:00","id":504929,"title":"","content":"A DA Werewolf would be nice, I like the feel of it but I think the real story in DA Werewolf was poorly addressed. The main conflicts should be concerned with kinfolk both wolf and human. Kinfolk as a resource are absolutely necessary. The Nation is strong at this time Man is just rediscovering the ancient banes of the Werewolves. The Wyrm while growing stronger is arguably the weakest member of the triat. And multi tribal Septs should be rare really rare. Most conflict should be tribe against tribe along with threats to the kinfolk. Oh and vampires this should be the time when the Garou are actively and aggressively attacking the leeches. Mages as magic begins to change should be eyeing Caerns with envy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:26:10-07:00","id":504943,"title":"","content":"I would love for more dark ages books, particlarly ones that cover what the fera were doing, more Dark ages mage. I would adore it if there was a dark ages mage india and china book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:37:26-07:00","id":504948,"title":"","content":"India as a whole has never been covered properly. I would like to see the region covered in both Dark Ages and Modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:21:44-07:00","id":505153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=504682#post504682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is good setting-wise, but suffers from the problem of reducing an entire range of magic withing a pardigm to four pillars, means that the overlap of capabilities is MASSIVE. To make characters more distinct, I'd make knowing specific &quot;spells&quot; (rotes) actually matter, thus playing up the studying magical lore element of the setting. Basically I'd rip off DA: Fae a bit, and make spells you know easier and safer, while creative casting has huge backlash risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is extra versatality of the Pillars and the fact that the reinforce the paradigms. You will still have different spells and effects based on your personal interpretation and preference. I've actually found the whole DA system quite a bit more evocative and in service to the actual ideas behind Mage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T06:56:23-07:00","id":505394,"title":"","content":"So here's something to keep in mind: just because something got covered one way by a DA book in the past doesn't mean that it has to get covered the exact same way by the DA books of the future. We already know that OP is willing to break the mold on some things (for example, rather than just reprinting KotE, there are going to be new African bloodlines of vampires separated from the history of Caine, if not in VDA20 then in another DA title). Hell, before that, White Wolf had no problem occasionally retconning particular aspects, ESPECIALLY with regards to non-European/non-US based things (Kindred of the East outright replaced the original conception of Eastern vampires about four or five years after the Gaki and the Cats were published, though there were enough similarities to say that the Gaki were how the western Vampires saw the Kuei-jin; Ebony Kingdom expanded upon the African vampires from a single Laibon bloodline into a more extensive, if admittedly derivative field; and while there were reasons for the change in their powers in-universe, we saw a very different portrayal of mummies and their powers in M:tR as in the original and revised Mummy books, due to how the world and the system had evolved). Just because the Djinn were portrayed in one book as Spirits of the Middle East, doesn't mean they can't be altered into the Fae of the Cradle of Civilization, or into something else entirely (and if the difference between Djinn and Fae like the difference between Fae and the Changelings of the East, I'm honestly all for it - it's novelty and a new approach).<br /> <br /> As for Wrath DA - again, just because in the past the mechanics of Wraith simply had to be ported back in time, doesn't mean a supplement couldn't be interesting, useful, and innovative. I'm not a big Wraith fan overall, but there are DA-related elements that Wraith can explore, if not in a full adaptation a la VDA20, then in an historical-themed era book that looks at new unique Wraith-related threats. Did the Fisher Heretics have new arcanoi that were lost to time afterwards to both sides? What about the victims of the Black Plague? How did the rampant surge of plague dead affect the Underworld and its politics?<br /> <br /> As for Mage DA20: I wholly welcome it, with the Pillars and all. I agree with Asmodai on the idea that they help reinforce the paradigm concept and add an interesting, different feel to the game. My only hope is that there's more expansion into the Crafts of the Dark Ages, both European and otherwise (a look at what the early Wu Keng looked like using Pillars, or the Wu Lung, or mages in Africa and the Americas, would be worth the price of admission on its own).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:41:37-07:00","id":505458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=505394#post505394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's something to keep in mind: just because something got covered one way by a DA book in the past doesn't mean that it has to get covered the exact same way by the DA books of the future. We already know that OP is willing to break the mold on some things (for example, rather than just reprinting KotE, there are going to be new African bloodlines of vampires separated from the history of Caine, if not in VDA20 then in another DA title). Hell, before that, White Wolf had no problem occasionally retconning particular aspects, ESPECIALLY with regards to non-European/non-US based things (Kindred of the East outright replaced the original conception of Eastern vampires about four or five years after the Gaki and the Cats were published, though there were enough similarities to say that the Gaki were how the western Vampires saw the Kuei-jin; Ebony Kingdom expanded upon the African vampires from a single Laibon bloodline into a more extensive, if admittedly derivative field; and while there were reasons for the change in their powers in-universe, we saw a very different portrayal of mummies and their powers in M:tR as in the original and revised Mummy books, due to how the world and the system had evolved). Just because the Djinn were portrayed in one book as Spirits of the Middle East, doesn't mean they can't be altered into the Fae of the Cradle of Civilization, or into something else entirely (and if the difference between Djinn and Fae like the difference between Fae and the Changelings of the East, I'm honestly all for it - it's novelty and a new approach).<br /> <br /> As for Wrath DA - again, just because in the past the mechanics of Wraith simply had to be ported back in time, doesn't mean a supplement couldn't be interesting, useful, and innovative. I'm not a big Wraith fan overall, but there are DA-related elements that Wraith can explore, if not in a full adaptation a la VDA20, then in an historical-themed era book that looks at new unique Wraith-related threats. Did the Fisher Heretics have new arcanoi that were lost to time afterwards to both sides? What about the victims of the Black Plague? How did the rampant surge of plague dead affect the Underworld and its politics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages V20 is 1242. The bubonic plague epidemic was post-1347, so it's slightly more than a century off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:18:44-07:00","id":505680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=504948#post504948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">India as a whole has never been covered properly. I would like to see the region covered in both Dark Ages and Modern times.</div> </div> </div> </div>agreed, but i also would like to see more of the traditions/crafts with dark ages versions to use. I want to see all of them with the pillar system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:43:49-07:00","id":505754,"title":"","content":"Here is my list for the DA: Mage line if it ever gets renewed:<br /> A books (or a series of books) that detail the other places than Europe such as the Middle East and North Africa/South Spain, India, China, Africa, perhaps even the Americas. This would be the ideal place to introduce the Akashics, Chakravanti, Seers of Cronos and others.<br /> <br /> Fellowship books. Books that really goes into detail about the diffrent Fellowships, Mostly because i want to read more about the OoH in this time, with lots and lots of Pillar based Rotes. That's one thing i felt missing from the OoH in DA: Mage, rotes. All the other fellowships got lots and lots of rotes but not the OoH. Each of the Fellowshipbooks should also give examples of magic that could be considered wierd by the Fellowship (Teleporting and scrying for the OoH for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":392,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","user":"Cadmiumcadamium","date":". 05-06-2015, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T15:30:16-07:00","id":506136,"title":"","content":"Non-European books for Dark Ages would be sexy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:10:19-07:00","id":506352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=505754#post505754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my list for the DA: Mage line if it ever gets renewed:<br /> A books (or a series of books) that detail the other places than Europe such as the Middle East and North Africa/South Spain, India, China, Africa, perhaps even the Americas. This would be the ideal place to introduce the Akashics, Chakravanti, Seers of Cronos and others.<br /> <br /> Fellowship books. Books that really goes into detail about the diffrent Fellowships, Mostly because i want to read more about the OoH in this time, with lots and lots of Pillar based Rotes. That's one thing i felt missing from the OoH in DA: Mage, rotes. All the other fellowships got lots and lots of rotes but not the OoH. Each of the Fellowshipbooks should also give examples of magic that could be considered wierd by the Fellowship (Teleporting and scrying for the OoH for example).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here is a question should there be new fellowships for the rest of the world as in not just a medieval version of the current traditions, like the norse Valdermann and if so what should they be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:38:09-07:00","id":506364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=505153#post505153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the point is extra versatality of the Pillars and the fact that the reinforce the paradigms. You will still have different spells and effects based on your personal interpretation and preference. I've actually found the whole DA system quite a bit more evocative and in service to the actual ideas behind Mage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's definite word crunch though that results in 4 ridiculously broad pillars for each, when in a perfect world, each would have a greater number of narrower (relatively speaking) pillars, so different members of the same Fellowships have more distinct magical knowledge from each other without needing to branch outside of their paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:20:43-07:00","id":508143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=506364#post506364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's definite word crunch though that results in 4 ridiculously broad pillars for each, when in a perfect world, each would have a greater number of narrower (relatively speaking) pillars, so different members of the same Fellowships have more distinct magical knowledge from each other without needing to branch outside of their paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we know you CAN have more than 4, sorta, at least, that's how the Craftmason's seem to sorta/kinda be.<br /> <br /> Rotes that actually have some tie in to the way the rules work instead of running the gambit to simple explanations for simple effects to impossible impossible based on the Pillars allegedly used with no real underlying mechanical rhyme or reason. Either Rotes should DO something, cost something, BE something, have some kind of bonus built in (other than being impossible based on the Pillars or a -1 Diff) or just have them down as examples: &quot;Pillar X 3 does THIS, Pillar Y 2/Pillar x 3 does THAT&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that would also be nice for Mage non-DA as well....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:28:01-07:00","id":510696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support#post494360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What books would you like to see for expanding to existing Dark Ages lines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a ByNight.<br /> Costantinople ByNight was awesome, and I want more!<br /> London By Night (for extension Great Britain, as London wasn't much of a city at that time but, hey, it got Mithras!), Rome by Night (cappadocians, old Inconnu, whatever else), Sicily By Night (Lasombra, whatever else and the incoming Gratiano), Carthago By Night (yep, I mean it)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:03:05-07:00","id":513278,"title":"","content":"I would rather prefer keeping the Fae and Djinn as separate supernaturals and I wholly support a gameline splat based on Djinn.<br /> <br /> In a matter of fact, I would like to see DA: Fae expanded on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","user":"TunnelsofDarkness","date":". 05-13-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:09:41-07:00","id":515847,"title":"","content":"The Black Plague wold make for a good setting book. The amount of plague victims really going to mess with the Vampire's feeding stock and any land they hold. The Celestial Chorus would be busy trying to help these poor souls though faith healing and what to do when their Jewish members are getting persecuted. The Ratkin bragging it was because of them and what trouble could come if some outsider was to hear it (example: Garou, Inquisitors, the Prince of the city, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:14:42-07:00","id":516233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/494360-if-dark-ages-got-returning-support?p=515847#post515847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Plague wold make for a good setting book. The amount of plague victims really going to mess with the Vampire's feeding stock and any land they hold. The Celestial Chorus would be busy trying to help these poor souls though faith healing and what to do when their Jewish members are getting persecuted. The Ratkin bragging it was because of them and what trouble could come if some outsider was to hear it (example: Garou, Inquisitors, the Prince of the city, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like it would be really really grim, but probably the more interesting for all that. Kinda like it would have been a Black Dog imprint back in the day. <br /> <br /> I can definitely see some blame going around among vampires and the blame getting heaped on the Malkavians, Nosferatu and Tremere, probably leading to purges such as happened to many Jewish ghettos at the time. Some nice rules about the effects of feeding on the diseased, dying and dead would be appropriate. Along with a possible supernatural component to the Death as well?<br /> <br /> It could be an interesting point to see the Messianic Voices start or complete a fission into the Cabal of Pure Thought, for whom the plague was a judgement from God with the logical outcome being that everyone needs to start worshiping the CORRECT way to prevent further scourging from on high, and the Celestial Chorus, who would be doing more of what you said (and probably dying right left and center as well). I have a hard time with seeing Jewish mages, on the whole, being a part of that group of &quot;faith-based&quot; mages. The sub-groups that would later become the Traditions are much more fragmented and less ecumenical. The very name &quot;Messianic Voices&quot; argues that classic Jewish mysticism would be out of place. What Jewish mages there were would have to somewhat eschatalogical, looking forward to a Messiah who has not yet come instead of backwards to the done deeds of one from over a millennium before. Which would probably be a source of friction. I can definitely see Lions of Zion frantically trying to defend their people, perhaps with some actions that presage Rabbi Loew and the Golem of Prague. You might also get examples of Verbena/Old Faith-ers using rose and posies to effectively ward against the disease... Hermetics slamming their Chantry doors and refusing to see anyone.... Etc. <br /> <br /> I need to dig through my stuff, but did the Garou think the Ratkin were even around so much? It seems like admitting they did a shoddy job during the War of Rage.... I think it would be much cooler if they did know the Ratkin were in those human cesspools called &quot;cities&quot; that any REAL Garou avoid unless it's time for some culling (sorry, Warders, but you know it's true).<br /> <br /> And I need someone who is more in tune with what was going on with the Fae at that point to know if it's just Commoners to worry about. The Firstborn are gone, right? Maybe this was the breaking down point of European Inanimae/Changeling relations? Most Inanimae couldn't care less about a bunch of humans die as long it's not their stream that gets polluted with piles of festering corpses, etc. vs. the Changelings who are seeing all the humans die around them (and dying themselves) and ask for help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T00:23:01-07:00","id":516827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\">PookaKnight</a></b> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#696969\">I suspect that if DA: Fae gets revisited it'll be similar to how V20 Dark Ages is a V20 supplement instead of the core book for a Dark Ages game line. That being said, I also hope that it doesn't change too much about the setup of DA: Fae. I like that it presents Fae society before the shattering but are confused about the new found power humans seem to have which any Changeling: The Dreaming fan can immediately recognize as the rise of banality during the sundering. My only compliant is that I wish it tied into established C:tD history a little better. There's no mention of the Fomorians or the noble houses for example. The DA: Fae scenario in Darkening Sky, despite my dislike of it as a pre-made adventure, the trigger for the Shattering was brilliant. Hopefully, if future DA: Fae material is a C20 supplement, it'll tie into C:tD's established history a bit better. </span></i> </div> </div> </div>Well, Now that Mage is riding alongside Vampire and getting its own Victorian Age book, may Changeling could get a similar setting to fill those empty spaces, too. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T17:03:24-07:00","id":661251,"title":"","content":"Bumping this due to some discusion in the vampire forms about v20 Dark Ages<br /> Some things I would like is looking at the medieval world but from the point of view of the other splats. As an example for Dark Ages Mage, talking about the church and how mages work with the medieval church. The Fae and Chivilary and so on. This was done for vampire with things like the Ashen Knight, but I want to see more in how the other splats work with the medieval world. <br /> <br /> I also would like region books, baiscaly books like Transylvania by Night but for other Game lines in Addition to Vampire. So for instance Rajaput by Night, Rage across the Holy Roman Empire, Mage of Iberia/Al-Andalus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}